IMPORTANT: This is a real environment with shell and network access. Investigate with tools — do not guess or simulate.

## Make server: MCP only

For Make server work (custom apps, modules, RPCs, functions, connections, scenarios, data stores):
- Use Make MCP tools only. Never call Make REST from shell (no curl/Invoke-WebRequest with API keys from settings).
- If MCP returns auth, login, 401, or 403 errors: stop after at most 2 attempts, tell me clearly that Make access failed, and ask me to fix MCP login. Do not retry with shell, alternate endpoints, or workarounds in a loop.

## Verify before claiming

Before stating API endpoints, fields, enums, module contents, review findings, or that something is missing/wrong:
- Read the actual local files, or fetch the live app or vendor spec via MCP/download.
- Never rely on training data, old chat context, or stale files when correctness matters.
- If you have not verified, say so explicitly. Do not invent comments, code, or spec details.

## Make app changes: ask first

- Do not create new functions, RPCs, webhooks, or server-side modules unless I explicitly asked.
- Do not fix, deploy, or delete unless I asked. Default: investigate thoroughly, report root cause and proposed fix, then ask if I should apply it.
- Server and public app components are hard to delete — treat new components as irreversible without my approval.
- Never delete or replace components I said are already published.

## Make custom function code

- One top-level function per file; nest helpers inside it (no sibling top-level functions).
- Use modern JavaScript: const/let, arrow functions, .map()/.filter()/.forEach() — avoid var and manual index loops unless matching existing app style.
- Reuse existing functions in the app before adding new logic or new functions.

## Make SDK app files

When editing Make custom (SDK) app files locally or via MCP (`*.iml.json`, `makecomapp.json`, connections, functions, webhooks, etc.):
- Never minify. Keep files as pretty-printed JSONC — multi-line, indented, with `//` comments where the file already uses them.
- Edit only the keys/lines that need to change; do not run a formatter over the whole file or rewrite it single-line.
- If a file is already minified, leave its style unchanged unless I ask to reformat it.

## Failure handling and scope

- Same error twice with the same cause → stop and report. Do not keep trying variants.
- After edits, verify they landed (re-read the file or re-fetch via MCP) before saying done.
- When a skill or command applies, follow it — do not reinvent the workflow.
- Stay within what I asked; if scope is unclear, ask before expanding.

## Shell vs MCP (general)

- Shell is for local files, git, vendor OpenAPI downloads, and workspace scripts — not for authenticated Make server API calls.
- For vendor APIs outside Make, download or fetch real documentation before designing parameters or URLs.
